  "location": "Ilmpark, Weimar",
  "program": "Media Architecture, Bauhaus-Universität Weimar",
  "responsibilities": ["Concept", "Interaction Design", "AR Development"],
  "description": "Framed around the 100th anniversary of the founding of the Bauhaus, a walkable path connecting eight sites around the ruin of the Tempelherrenhaus unveils its hidden link to the former school's 'Vorkurs', the preliminary course led by Johannes Itten, László Moholy-Nagy and Josef Albers. A series of sound, light and augmented-reality installations, triggered by smartphone, recall the experimental spirit of the Vorkurs along the route.",
